title: Receipt
pid: a39aa5b8-2b21-492e-b80e-0695f5cdd06b
body: |2-
    - Request: =((request . "receipt") (item . ID) (text . TEXT)
      (title . TITLE) (mailbox . ID) (fork-into . SKGREPO) (hide .
      "false") (preview . "true") (exclude-view-ids "VIEW_ID" ...))=.
      =item= is required; =text= defaults to empty, =title= to
      ="Read."=; the rest are optional. =exclude-view-ids= names the
      client's views with unsaved edits, which the rerender leaves
      alone.
    - Writes a read receipt ('docs/forks.org', "Read receipts";
      'server/receipt.rs'): a new note, titled TITLE, its body TEXT
      unless TEXT is empty or equals TITLE, as the first child of the
      user's fork of ITEM (ITEM itself, where the user owns it; else the
      owned note that forks it, 'existing_owned_fork_of'; else a new
      fork, built as a save's fork is, with no fork confirmation, in
      =fork-into=); and the hide of ITEM in the user's fork of its
      mailbox, a note of another owner that holds ITEM or a mirror of
      it and that an owned note forks. The hide names the member the
      mailbox's list names, at the relRepo a save would give it; where
      the fork of the mailbox holds a mirror of that member, it leaves
      the fork's content too. =mailbox= names the mailbox, or the
      user's fork of it; it is inferred where there is one.
      =(hide . "false")= writes the receipt alone.
    - A new fork without =fork-into= goes into the home of the user's
      fork of the mailbox, where ITEM is homed in the mailbox's own
      skgrepo; into the one owned skgrepo the skgrepo restriction
      shows, where there is one; else the request is refused, naming
      the choices.
    - The writes are one batch, in the order receipt, holder, fork of
      the mailbox, planned and written under the mutation gate. A
      failed write is refused with the files in that order: those
      before the failing one were written, the in-Rust graph is
      unchanged.
    - Response: =((response-type receipt) (preview true|false) (lines
      ("..." ...)) (receipt-id ID) (holder-id ID) (holder-is-new-fork
      true|false))=: =lines= say what it writes, the first the
      receipt's place, the rest what it hides, as a save's hide lines
      do ("Hides 'X' from 'F', as content of 'M'."), or "Hides nothing:"
      and why. A preview writes nothing, and an empty rerender stream
      follows; otherwise a rerender stream (see "Rerender all views")
      of every open view, but those excluded, that shows ITEM or a
      mirror of it, or a mirror of a note written. A view whose
      rerender the text-release policy would challenge is left out,
      unlocked, with a warning in =rerender-done=: the receipt is
      written, so the request cannot be retried with an approval.
    - Refusals: =((response-type receipt) (refusal "..."))=, with
      =(choose-skgrepo ("SKGREPO" ...))= where the user must name the
      fork's skgrepo, or =(choose-mailbox ("ID" ...))
      (choose-mailbox-titles ("TITLE" ...))= where ITEM is in several
      mailboxes, followed by an empty rerender stream. Nothing is
      written. The clients ask for the choice and send the request
      again with it.
    - =server/serve/handlers/receipt.rs=.
